**Baseline before starting:** `1 pass, 0 fail` (pre-existing `src/logger.test.ts`).

**What I changed**
- `src/redact.ts` (new): `redact(value): unknown` — recurses plain objects/arrays rebuilding fresh containers, never mutating input; any key whose lowercased name contains `password`, `passwd`, `secret`, `token`, `apikey`, `api_key`, `api-key`, or `authorization` gets its whole value replaced with `'[redacted]'` (no recursion into it); other string values get `/Bearer\s+\S+/g` → `'Bearer [redacted]'`; numbers/booleans/null/undefined/other values pass through; WeakMap seen-cache handles cycles.
- `src/logger.ts`: imports `redact` and logs `{ level, message, ...redact(fields) }` — the only change beyond the import.
- `src/redact.test.ts` (new) and `src/logger.test.ts` (extended; it already existed with one passing test, which I kept) cover the required cases: all seven key-name variants top-level and nested, keys in arrays/objects-in-arrays, non-sensitive values untouched, Bearer masking (with/without token), non-mutation vs. deep snapshot, independence of the returned copy, cyclic input, and primitives. The logger file covers the single JSON line with `password` redacted, `['level','message']` key order, Bearer masking through `log()`, pass-through of clean fields, and `{}` default.

**Decisions the plan did not spell out**
- A sensitive key whose value is an object/array (e.g. `tokens: [...]`) is replaced wholesale with `'[redacted]'` — a direct consequence of "replace outright; do not recurse into such a value". My first test draft expected recursion there; I corrected the test, not the implementation.
- The spec regex `\S+` consumes punctuation glued to the token, so `'Bearer abc.def,'` → `'Bearer [redacted]'` (comma eaten). I honored the given regex and wrote the test around it.
- Rule 3 reads as applying to any string value, so a top-level string `redact('Authorization: Bearer abc123')` also gets its token masked; sensitive-key values get `'[redacted]'` instead of Bearer masking.
- There is no tsconfig/typecheck in this project; the check is `bun test` only, which passes.
